 "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 6837, "total_tokens": 6837}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Cloud Integration and Data Services Overview as of September 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's Cloud Integration and Data Services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around September 2025.\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services Updates\n\nCloud Integration for Data Services has undergone several updates, including the removal of 'DSOD' from the URL, the introduction of a new type of user for agent registration, and the compilation of security recommendations. These updates aim to enhance security and user experience, ensuring seamless integration and data management. [Data: Sources (45, 46, 48), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 19), (2025, 09, 25))]\n\n## Deprecation of Microsoft Azure Data Lake Storage Gen1\n\nMicrosoft Azure Data Lake Storage Gen1 was retired on February 29, 2024, and SAP Cloud Integration for Data Services will end support for Gen1 in an early 2026 release. Users are recommended to migrate to Gen2 for continued support and data integrity. [Data: Source (50), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 29), (2025, 09, 25))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has seen several updates, including the addition of client certificate and key support for CPT and the deprecation of several operators. These updates aim to enhance security and user experience, ensuring seamless integration and data management. [Data: Sources (180, 255), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 20))]", "# SAP Data Intelligence and ABAP Environment Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components focusing on Data Intelligence and ABAP Environment, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide data management and development tools effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Data Intelligence Operational Scope\n\nSAP Data Intelligence plays a pivotal role in providing data management capabilities, including data transfer, support for various data sources, and deprecated operators. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential data management pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving data management standards. Effective data management not only prevents data anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3068, 3070), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 20))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Development Tools\n\nThe ABAP Environment provides development tools for Eclipse, including ABAP SQL Consumption Model, ADT Links in IDE Action HTML Results, Creating and Editing CDS Table Entities, and Creating and Editing Electronic Document Consistency Scenarios. These tools enable customers and partners to create consistency scenarios, check the consistency of business documents across systems, and create and maintain launchpad app descriptor items. [Data: Sources (836, 837, 838), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 16), (2025, 05, 16))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Data Management\n\nCollaboration between SAP Data Intelligence and ABAP Environment ensures that data management capabilities are integrated with development tools, providing a holistic approach to data management and development. This synergy is vital for SAP's operational stability and innovation, and has been instrumental in aligning the company's strategies with data management and development standards. [Data: Sources (3068, 3070), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 20))]", "# SAP Data Intelligence and Task Center Updates Overview as of April 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes in SAP Data Intelligence and Task Center as of April 2024. The information highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and security of these platforms, ensuring seamless operations and compliance with regulatory standards.\n\n## Enhanced Security Measures in SAP Data Intelligence\n\nSAP Data Intelligence has introduced key pair authentication for Snowflake connections, enhancing security and protecting sensitive data. This update ensures that data is transmitted securely, reducing the risk of unauthorized access and data breaches. The implementation of key pair authentication is a significant step towards maintaining the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in SAP Data Intelligence [Data: Sources (726), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 20))].\n\n## Interoperability and Compatibility Updates in SAP Data Intelligence\n\nSAP Data Intelligence has updated its libraries and components to ensure seamless interoperability and compatibility with other systems. The updates include the Go libraries, Kafka operators, and R versions, which are crucial for maintaining the integrity and efficiency of data processing and analysis. These updates enable customers to take advantage of the latest features and capabilities in SAP Data Intelligence, ensuring that their systems remain up-to-date and compliant with regulatory standards [Data: Sources (3083, 3084, 3085), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 20))].\n\n## New Features and Functionality in SAP Task Center\n\nSAP Task Center has introduced new features and functionality, including public views, which enable users to access predefined views and improve collaboration and productivity. Additionally, the platform has updated its HTML5 apps, which may require users to clear their browser cache and refresh their browser to ensure seamless operations [Data: Sources (3087, 3088), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 19), (2024, 04, 19))].\n\n## Application Autoscaler Updates in Cloud Foundry\n\nCloud Foundry has introduced a new metric type called cpuutil, which enables users to set scaling rules based on CPU entitlement. This update allows users to specify thresholds with values from 0% to 100%, eliminating the need to calculate CPU entitlement for their applications [Data: Sources (3089), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 18), (2024, 04, 18))].\n\n## Java Server Updates in Neo Environment\n\nThe Java Server in the Neo environment has been updated to Tomcat version 9.0.87, which is a significant improvement over the previous version. This update is recommended for all users to ensure seamless operations and compliance with regulatory standards [Data: Sources (3090), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 18), (2024, 04, 18))].", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## Identity Provisioning Operational Scope\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing user identities and access control. Their proactive approach, highlighted in 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2291, 2298), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 10), (2024, 09, 11))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP have been upgraded in 2024, introducing new features and improvements. These updates enhance the overall user experience, improve security, and increase efficiency. The regular upgrades demonstrate SAP's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (2293, 2295), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 10), (2024, 09, 11))]\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service component at SAP has undergone significant enhancements in 2024, addressing critical issues and improving overall performance. These updates ensure accurate pricing calculations, prevent errors, and enhance the customer experience. The Pricing Service plays a vital role in SAP's operations, and these enhancements demonstrate the company's focus on quality and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (2818, 2819), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 04), (2024, 06, 05))]", "# Joule and SAP Ecosystem Overview as of March 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the Joule and SAP ecosystem, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP ecosystem's operations around March 2025.\n\n## Joule Component Overview\n\nJoule is a key component of the SAP ecosystem, providing data management and security capabilities. Its updates and releases have a significant impact on the ecosystem's operations. Joule's support for various file formats, including JPEG, JPG, PNG, and TIFF, enhances data management capabilities [Data: Sources (75, 1162), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 10), (2025, 03, 27))].\n\n## SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition Updates\n\nSAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition has received significant updates, including support for navigational and transactional capabilities in FPS02 and FPS01. These updates enhance the ecosystem's operational capabilities and improve user experience [Data: Sources (73, 1162), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 25), (2025, 03, 27))].\n\n## Data Center Availability\n\nJoule is now available in multiple data centers, including Microsoft Azure and AWS. This expansion enhances the ecosystem's data management capabilities and improves user experience [Data: Sources (76, 77), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 07), (2025, 01, 30))].\n\n## Roles-Based Access Control\n\nJoule has introduced roles-based access control for the standalone web client, enhancing security and user experience. This update ensures that users can only access the client with the required roles assigned [Data: Source (78), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 29), (2025, 01, 29))].\n\n## Conversational Experience Upgrade\n\nSAP SuccessFactors has upgraded its conversational experience, introducing a new transactional use case and enhancing user experience. This update reflects the ecosystem's focus on improving user experience and operational capabilities [Data: Source (79), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 17), (2025, 01, 17))].\n\n## Component Version Updates\n\nMultiple components, including SAP HANA Cloud, Java Server, and Document Management Service, have received version updates. These updates enhance the ecosystem's operational capabilities and improve user experience [Data: Sources (1166, 1167, 1168), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 24), (2025, 03, 25))].", "# Joule and SAP Ecosystem Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the Joule and SAP ecosystem, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP ecosystem's operations around 2025.\n\n## Joule's Operational Scope\n\nJoule is a key component of the SAP ecosystem, providing data management and integration capabilities. Its proactive approach to supporting various SAP components, such as SAP S/4HANA Cloud, SAP SuccessFactors, and SAP Task Center, helps ensure seamless data exchange and efficient operations. Effective data management not only prevents data anomalies but also supports the SAP ecosystem's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (71, 72, 73, 74, 75), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 26))]\n\n## SAP Ecosystem Updates\n\nThe SAP ecosystem has undergone significant updates in 2025, with various components receiving new features and improvements. For example, SAP S/4HANA Cloud has introduced new use cases, while SAP SuccessFactors has upgraded its conversational experience. These updates underscore the commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (1441, 1442, 1443, 1444, 1445), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 11), (2025, 02, 11))]\n\n## Intercomponent Collaboration\n\nCollaboration between various SAP components, such as Joule, SAP Task Center, and SAP Build Process Automation, ensures that data management, integration, and automation strategies are aligned. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating various SAP components. Enhanced intercomponent cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the SAP ecosystem's strategies with customer needs. [Data: Sources (71, 1446, 1450), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 11))]", "# Joule and SAP Ecosystem Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the Joule and SAP ecosystem, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP ecosystem's operations and development around 2025.\n\n## Joule's Key Features and Updates\n\nJoule is a key component of the SAP ecosystem, offering various features and updates. Notable updates include support for new use cases, document grounding capabilities, and improved accessibility. These enhancements demonstrate Joule's commitment to supporting the SAP ecosystem's growth and development. [Data: Sources (71, 72, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 26))]\n\n## SAP SuccessFactors Integration\n\nSAP SuccessFactors has been integrated with Joule, enabling the introduction of new transactional use cases and the upgrade of existing ones. This integration demonstrates the SAP ecosystem's focus on human resources and employee experience. [Data: Sources (72, 79, 1539), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 17), (2025, 01, 27))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Continuous Integration & Delivery\n\nKyma Runtime and Continuous Integration & Delivery are critical components of the SAP ecosystem, supporting the development and deployment of applications. Notable updates include the deprecation of outdated tools and the introduction of new features, such as increased quotas and support for new file types. [Data: Sources (1531, 1533, 1534, 1535, 1536), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 16), (2025, 01, 28))]", "# Joule and SAP Ecosystem Overview as of March 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the Joule and SAP ecosystem, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP ecosystem's operations around March 2025.\n\n## Joule's Role in the SAP Ecosystem\n\nJoule is a key component in the SAP ecosystem, enabling users to view business data, create insights cards, and support various use cases. Its capabilities are essential for data management and analytics within the SAP ecosystem. Joule's updates, such as supporting new file formats and data centers, demonstrate its commitment to improving user experience and expanding its reach within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (71, 75), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 26))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps and Task Center Updates\n\nSAP Build Apps and Task Center have introduced new features, such as a date field with input component and a guided tour on getting started. These updates aim to enhance user experience and improve application development within the SAP ecosystem. The new property for extending the maximum pull period in Task Center demonstrates its focus on scalability and flexibility. [Data: Sources (1141, 1143), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 27))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and SAP Document AI Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has updated its Istio module to version 1.15.0, enabling custom metrics collection and improving observability. SAP Document AI has introduced new features, such as support for documents in JPEG, JPG, PNG, and TIFF file formats. These updates demonstrate the commitment of these components to improving user experience and expanding their capabilities within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (1148, 1149), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 26))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of March 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their operational scope, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape around March 2025.\n\n## SAP Build Apps Operational Scope\n\nSAP Build Apps at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing a low-code development platform for building web and mobile applications. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective use of SAP Build Apps not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (168), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 27), (2025, 03, 27))]\n\n## Joule Operational Scope\n\nJoule at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing a low-code development platform for building business applications. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective use of Joule not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1145, 1146), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 26), (2025, 03, 26))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP's technology components, established in 2025, ensures that technological advancements are aligned with regulatory requirements. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1148), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 12), (2025, 03, 26))]", "# Joule and SAP S/4HANA Cloud Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and features of Joule and SAP S/4HANA Cloud, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide enhanced functionality and support for various business processes. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Joule's Operational Scope\n\nJoule is a key component of SAP S/4HANA Cloud, providing various transactional, navigational, and informational use cases to support business processes. Its capabilities include document grounding, business partner certificate management, and supplier invoice management, among others. Joule's integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud enables seamless data exchange and enhances the overall user experience. Effective use of Joule's capabilities can improve business efficiency and reduce operational costs. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 23), (2025, 09, 25))]\n\n## SAP S/4HANA Cloud Features and Functionality\n\nSAP S/4HANA Cloud is a cloud-based enterprise resource planning (ERP) system that provides a range of features and functionalities to support various business processes. Its integration with Joule enables the use of various transactional, navigational, and informational use cases, including product lifecycle management, cash and liquidity management, and sales management. SAP S/4HANA Cloud's cloud-based architecture provides scalability, flexibility, and reduced maintenance costs. Effective use of SAP S/4HANA Cloud's features and functionalities can improve business efficiency and competitiveness. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 22), (2025, 09, 23))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Business Process Support\n\nCollaboration between Joule and SAP S/4HANA Cloud enables seamless data exchange and enhances the overall user experience. This synergy is vital for holistic business process support and has been instrumental in integrating various business processes at the company. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with business requirements. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 22), (2025, 09, 23))]", "# Joule Over